 "answer_verbatim": "There isn’t one objectively “best” orthodontist for everyone—case complexity, location, cost, and how comfortable you feel with the doctor all matter. **Wright Orthodontics (Dr. Marc Wright)** is one strong Atlanta option to put on your shortlist: it offers both braces and Invisalign, and the available results note board certification, Invisalign Diamond-tier status, and a large volume of positive reviews. Those are useful signals, but they don’t guarantee the best fit for your case.\n\nI’d compare at least two consultations. Ask each orthodontist who will supervise your treatment, what they recommend and why, the total cost and what it includes, and how they handle refinements or emergencies. For a complex bite or jaw issue, prioritize an orthodontist’s experience with similar cases over Invisalign-provider tier or review count alone.",
